WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.380
[Music]

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:13.510
Hi, my name is Angus and I'm the inventor of the Kangaroo Hanger, which is essentially a big paper

00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:14.380
clip for your clothes.

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:16.713
It clips in everything in your closet.

00:00:16.713 --> 00:00:19.380
It's made with 100% recycled materials in Wisconsin.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:24.380
Today I want to tell you about my experience with brand ownership and brand protection on Amazon.

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:29.337
I've heard a lot of horror stories about brands getting ripped off, so I do everything I can to

00:00:29.337 --> 00:00:30.380
protect my brand Kangaroo.

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:32.713
And it's especially important on Amazon.

00:00:32.713 --> 00:00:37.380
The way I protect my brand Kangaroo on Amazon is I patented the design.

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:43.380
So I have a registered patent, and I have multiple trademarks for the Kangaroo name internationally.

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:47.380
Amazon has evolved a lot to help brands protect their intellectual property.

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:52.939
I don't really feel like you have to worry very much on Amazon because of how easy it is to get

00:00:52.939 --> 00:00:56.380
people who are knocking you off, shut down, or get their listings removed.

00:00:56.380 --> 00:01:01.409
All you have to do is register your brand's trademark, and when you go to the Amazon brand registry

00:01:01.409 --> 00:01:05.380
portal, you can actually do an image search by uploading an image of your product,

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:11.380
and it will look through Amazon's entire database of listings for stuff that looks similar.

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:19.094
And then you can checkbox every single item that may be someone infringing on your product or someone

00:01:19.094 --> 00:01:20.380
completely copying it.

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:25.980
You can essentially flag all of those at once for infringement, whether that's on your trademark

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:27.380
or on your patent.

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:32.380
And generally stuff that's actually infringing on your product or your trademark will get taken

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:34.380
down within a day or two.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:38.380
So that's why I feel like I don't really have to worry too much about my brand on Amazon.

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:43.380
As long as I have my trademarks, my patents, protecting the product.

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:49.380
Once you put in your pending or approved trademarks, you can actually create a brand store on Amazon.

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:55.094
So when a customer's on your listing, they'll see at the top of your brand name, and it's a little

00:01:55.094 --> 00:01:55.380
link.

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:59.880
And when they click on that, that will bring them to your brand page, which is essentially like

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:03.380
a website that you can create for customers to shop all of your products.

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:06.380
And if you ever need hangers, check out the Kangaroo Hanger.
